  "body": "At the same time, we should address some of the issues due to it operating on JavaScript objects, but not using JavaScript language to do so.\n\nWe should also move from \"neuter\" to \"detach\".\n\nhttps://github.com/dslomov/ecmascript-structured-clone has a setup created by @dslomov and I that I think we should adopt here. If TC39 at some point takes this definition over that's fine, but until then it can live in the HTML standard, we just need to define it better.\n\n@heycam, we might also need new hooks from IDL to make this all work. One thing for instance is a check whether an object that is to be transferred can be created in the targetRealm: https://github.com/w3c/webrtc-pc/pull/317.\n\nI'm interested in working on this (unless someone can point me to something more pressing).\n",
